      "problem": "Find the maximum value of the parabola $y=-4(x+5)^{2}-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The maximum value of the parabola is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola. \n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=-4(x+5)^{2}-3\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-5$ and $k=-3.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-5,-3),$ and its maximum value is $-3.$",
